rrogantly named  primary DC universe that featured the  ongoing Adventures of the present-day  heroes  meanwhile the Golden Age versions  politely allowed themselves to be called  earth 2 despite the fact that they came  first clearly there was only one thing  left to do a crossover Justice League of  America number 21 and 22 featured crisis  on earth  and crisis on earth-2 in which the  Justice League teamed up with their  golden age counterparts in the Justice  Society to battle for the fate of two  universes this kicked off two important  DC traditions first with the idea of an  annual Jael a JSA crossover which  continued for the next 20 years the  second was that almost all of these  crossovers which spread out through the  DC Multiverse were called a crisis  making that the shorthand word for a  threat that went beyond the scale of a  single universe eventually though things  spiraled to the point of being as big as  they possibly could in 1985 DC made a  very bold promise for their new series  worlds will live  worlds will die and the universe will  never be the same for the most part they  delivered with a year-long event called  crisis on Infinite Earths the company  was restructuring their entire  multiverse into a single streamlined  whole but rather than just rebooting all  the comics they made it part of a story  a villain called the anti-monitor who  presumably did not monitor things was  wiping out universes and the ones that  remained coalesced into a single unified  timeline in the process major characters  like the flash and Supergirl were killed  off with as much permanence as there can  be in superhero comics which is to say  they were dead for about 20 years before  they inevitably came back that wasn't  quite the end though the crisis brand  was so strong that DC kept it around  even after they bailed on the multiverse  another event devoted to fixing up the  complicated DC u timeline was called  zero hour crisis and time and there was  a modern-day JLA JSA team up against the  fifth dimension called crisis times five  in 2006 Infinite Crisis as its name  implies came along to perverse all the  changes and reintroduce the multiverse  the branding loomed large in the minds  of fans as the biggest world shattering  events in DC's long history one of the  things that makes the TV version of  crisis on Infinite Earths so interesting  is that it's following in the same  tradition as its comic-book counterparts  once arrows surprising success led to a  series of spin-offs and other shows  debuted in their own universes trying to  cash in on the massive popularity of  superheroes these days  seeing them team-up became inevitable  much like it had in the comics the idea  of an annual crossover quickly became a  tradition for the air overs it started  with Ollie Queens teaming up with a  flash for a couple of story arcs that  ran through the respective shows in 2014  and then a backdoor pilot for legends of  tomorrow the following year things  really started to pick up in 2016 that  March saw the Super Girl episode world's  finest which saw the flash vibrating his  way to super girls universe now called  earth 38 that then led to a full-on  three-part arrowverse super girl  crossover called invasion and then just  to cap things off March 2017 saw duet an  episode of flash where Supergirl showed  up for a singing dancing team-up that  took advantage of the Stars musical  theatre backgrounds with a few catchy  tunes I was singing for you know I name  anymore I mean it's worth noting that  both world's finest and Invasion were  both named after crossover comics the  long-running Superman Batman team-up  title and a 1988 event in which three  alien races invaded earth at the same  time respectively that tradition was  continued with crisis on Earth X which  like the comic it was named for featured  the introduction of a world ruled by  Nazis complete with an evil Supergirl it  turned out that earth axe was a secret  5