eroes like vibe mr. terrific  Black Canary killer frost and even more  obscure characters like gun-toting  weirdo Wild Dogs showing up in their  supporting casts there's also legends of  tomorrow with firestorm with the atom  white canary vixen and more Plus  Stapledon and John Constantine bringing  actor Matt Ryan back for the role after  the cancellation of Constantine and  brought in Western hero Jonah Hex in an  episode where a 12-foot tall Care Bear  fought a demon and of course we have  that woman outside of that specific  universe though the CW also has  Supergirl and the heroes of Earth 38  including cara danvers Jon Jones the  Martian Manhunter The Guardian the  masked heroic identity of Superman's pal  Jimmy Olsen the Legion of super-heroes a  team from the 31st century with a  sprawling roster all its own and you  know Superman and the network also airs  Black Lightning which features the title  care  along with his daughters Jennifer and  Anissa the heroines known as thunder and  lightning and grace Choi who was a  member of The Outsiders alongside  Thunder in the comics but wait there's  more those are just the shows going on  now before the current run of successful  shows the CW and its predecessors also  ran Smallville which started as a teen  drama focused on a younger Clark Kent  but ran for 10 years and wound up  including everyone from Hawkman to  Zatanna  in 2002 there was the short-lived birds  of prey another take on a female focused  Batman free Gotham City about Batman and  Catwoman daughter the Huntress Plus  Oracle and black Canary those are all in  play for TVs crisis on Infinite Earths  and that's just the heroes the stage is  set for crisis on Infinite Earths to hit  the airwaves in December and from  everything we know so far it's going to  be big one where the Nazis won World War  two when where Kennedy was never  assassinated one more where all of us  are evil been there it sucks we already  know that characters from Smallville are  